r: after the last element comes the first one again. For each element, return the first greater value you meet when walking forward (wrapping around), or `-1` if no greater value exists.\n\nValues can repeat.","constraints":["1 <= nums.length <= 1e4","-1e9 <= nums[i] <= 1e9"],"hints":["Wrapping around once is like scanning the array twice in a row.","Loop i from 0 to 2n − 1 using nums[i % n], with a monotonic stack of indices that still need an answer.","Only push indices during the first pass (i < n); the second pass only resolves them. Fill the answer with −1 first."],"explain":"The array wraps around. The first 1 is followed by 2; nothing in the array is larger than 2 (-1); the last 1 wraps around to the 2 at the start. The answer is `[2,-1,2]`."},
