"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\"]","[[],[74771],[74770],[74778],[74778],[74778],[74771],[74774]]"],"out":"[null,1,1,3,4,5,1,2]","g":1},{"in":["[\"StockSpanner\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\"]","[[],[58713],[28299],[100000],[68453],[9054],[83117],[81125],[40754]]"],"out":"[null,1,1,3,1,1,3,1,1]","g":1},{"in":["[\"StockSpanner\",\"next\",\"next\"]","[[],[1],[1]]"],"out":"[null,1,2]","g":1},{"in":["[\"StockSpanner\",\"next\"]","[[],[76283]]"],"out":"[null,1]","g":1},{"in":["[\"StockSpanner\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\"]","[[],[56038],[56038],[56038],[92662],[56038],[92662],[56038],[56038],[56038],[56038],[92662]]"],"out":"[null,1,2,3,4,1,6,1,2,3,4,11]","g":1},{"in":["[\"StockSpanner\",\"next\"]","[[],[59985]]"],"out":"[null,1]","g":1},{"in":["[\"StockSpanner\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\"]","[[],[99935],[99935],[99935],[14153],[99935],[99935],[14153]]"],"out":"[null,1,2,3,1,5,6,1]","g":1},{"in":["[\"StockSpanner\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\"]","[[],[12003],[100000],[463],[39699],[90207],[100000]]"],"out":"[null,1,2,1,2,3,6]","g":1},{"in":["[\"StockSpanner\",\"next\"]","[[],[16547]]"],"out":"[null,1]","g":1},{"in":["[\"StockSpanner\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\",\"next\"]","[[],[33831],[33831],[33831],[33831],[33834],[33834]]"],"out":"[null,1,2,3,4,5,6]","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#10:6763f6aee4bb5cef\"","perf":{"label":"100,000 prices","gen":"","call":"StockSpanner sp = new StockSpanner(); long sum = 0; for (int i = 0; i < 100000; i++) sum += sp.next(i < 50000 ? 100000 - i : i); Object r = sum;"},"refMs":10}],"lesson":"monotonic-stack","statement":"Design `StockSpanner`, which receives one stock price per day:\n\n- `StockSpanner()` creates the object,\n- `int next(int price)` records today's price and returns today's span: the number of consecutive days, ending with today and counting backwards, on which the price was less than or equal to today's price.\n\nFor prices `[7, 2, 1, 2]` the span on the last day is 4: 2, 1, 2 and today. The tests call the class with a list of operations and their arguments.","constraints":["1 <= price <= 1e5","At most 10^5 calls to next"],"hints":["Walking back day by day is O(n) per call. Which older days can you forget for good?","Once a higher price arrives, a lower earlier price can never stop a later span. Keep a stack of (price, span) pairs with decreasing prices.","On next(price), pop every pair with price ≤ today's and add their spans to today's span (which starts at 1), then push today. Amortised O(1)."],"explain":"Each span counts consecutive days, ending today, with a price at or below today's. 70 covers itself and 60 (2); 75 covers 75, 60, 70, 60 (4); 85 covers everything back to 80 (6). Output: `[null,1,1,1,2,1,4,6]`."},
{"slug":"remove-k-digits","title":"Remove K Digits","level":"Medium","summary":"Remove k digits from the number string num to make it as small as possible. Return it without leading zeros (\"0\" if empty).","method":"removeKdigits","params":[["String","num"],["int","k"]],"returns":"String","tests":[{"in":["\"1432219\"","3"],"out":"\"1219\""},{"in":["\"10200\"","1"],"out":"\"200\""},{"in":["\"10\"","2"],"out":"\"0\""},{"in":["\"112\"","1"],"out":"\"11\""},{"in":["\"123456\"","3"],"out":"\"123\""},{"in":["\"9\"","1"],"out":"\"0\""},{"in":["\"92929\"","2"],"out":"\"229\"","g":1},{"in":["\"34939863\"","8"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"333\"","2"],"out":"\"3\"","g":1},{"in":["\"2\"","1"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"0\"","1"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"203\"","1"],"out":"\"3\"","g":1},{"in":["\"66666666\"","8"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"10111111010\"","1"],"out":"\"111111010\"","g":1},{"in":["\"8181687\"","1"],"out":"\"181687\"","g":1},{"in":["\"6\"","1"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"999\"","3"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"110000111\"","7"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"9999999\"","7"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"22\"","1"],"out":"\"2\"","g":1},{"in":["\"5\"","1"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"1\"","1"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"444\"","2"],"out":"\"4\"","g":1},{"in":["\"550\"","1"],"out":"\"50\"","g":1},{"in":["\"103\"","3"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"2332002\"","2"],"out":"\"22002\"","g":1},{"in":["\"99999\"","1"],"out":"\"9999\"","g":1},{"in":["\"1101\"","4"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"99999999999999999999\"","20"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"11111001011\"","11"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"8\"","1"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"378\"","1"],"out":"\"37\"","g":1},{"in":["\"10\"","1"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"221\"","3"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"100\"","1"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"303\"","1"],"out":"\"3\"","g":1},{"in":["\"2110232011\"","3"],"out":"\"232011\"","g":1},{"in":["\"9999999999999999\"","1"],"out":"\"999999999999999\"","g":1},{"in":["\"99999\"","4"],"out":"\"9\"","g":1},{"in":["\"555555\"","6"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"1000001\"","1"],"out":"\"1\"","g":1},{"in":["\"33121022112\"","11"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"11\"","2"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"99999999999999999\"","12"],"out":"\"99999\"","g":1},{"in":["\"20001031\"","8"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":["\"7\"","1"],"out":"\"0\"","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#44296:aadc5217b273c96a\"","perf":{"label":"a 100,000-digit number, k = 50,000","gen":"String a0 = \"1\" + BCB.str(99999, \"0123456789\"); int a1 = 50000;"},"refMs":13}],"lesson":"monotonic-stack","anchor":"remove-k-digits--a-greedy-increasing-stack","statement":"`num` is a non-negative integer written as a string. Remove exactly `k` digits so that the remaining number is as small as possible, and return it as a string.\n\nThe result must not have leading zeros, and if nothing is left, return `\"0\"`.","constraints":["1 <= num.length <= 1e5","1 <= k <= num.length","`num` has only digits and no leading zeros (except the number \"0\")"],"hints":["The leftmost digits matter most. When a digit is followed by a smaller one, removing the larger digit helps the most.","Scan left to right with a stack: while k > 0 and the top is bigger than the current digit, pop it (that uses one removal).","If removals are left over at the end, remove from the end (the stack is non-decreasing). Then strip leading zeros and return \"0\" if empty."],"explain":"Removing 4, 3 and the first 2 (each a digit larger than the one after it) leaves \"1219\", the smallest possible number. So the answer is \"1219\"."},
{"slug":"sum-of-subarray-minimums","title":"Sum of Subarray Minimums","level":"Medium","summary":"Return the sum of min(sub) over every contiguous subarray, modulo 10^9 + 7.","method":"sumSubarrayMins","params":[["int[]","arr"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["[3,1,2,4]"],"out":"17"},{"in":["[11,81,94,43,3]"],"out":"444"},{"in":["[1]"],"out":"1"},{"in":["[2,2,2]"],"out":"12"},{"in":["[30000,29999,29998,30000]"],"out":"299986"},{"in":["[2,1]"],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["[1,2,1,2]"],"out":"12","g":1},{"in":["[1,1,2,1,1,1,3,3,1]"],"out":"52","g":1},{"in":["[22208,16499,10127,30000,16998,11143,10465,19320,8016,2788,18994,30000,1,6175,18032,5819,14237,24646,6311,1,1994,23902,30000,2903]"],"out":"928672","g":1},{"in":["[3]"],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["[20695,9693,11482,1904]"],"out":"78565","g":1},{"in":["[1,4825,12027,5155,30000,22711,26648,18810,1,8335,22179,7500,1,3574,18963,3035,29213,6886,20992,27518,25112,12946,30000,12127,27919,2025]"],"out":"1112263","g":1},{"in":["[10851,29136,20267]"],"out":"102223","g":1},{"in":["[3,3,1,2,1,3,3,1]"],"out":"49","g":1},{"in":["[1,1]"],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["[4346,11032,17650,28231]"],"out":"114011","g":1},{"in":["[5786]"],"out":"5786","g":1},{"in":["[2]"],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["[23526,23528]"],"out":"70580","g":1},{"in":["[10572,10574,10574]"],"out":"63438","g":1},{"in":["[22456]"],"out":"22456","g":1},{"in":["[1,2]"],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["[2,3,2,2,1,1,3,1]"],"out":"49","g":1},{"in":["[12636,1,3732]"],"out":"16372","g":1},{"in":["[3,2,1,2,2,3,3,1,1]"],"out":"62","g":1},{"in":["[26471,26474,26473]"],"out":"158833","g":1},{"in":["[16315,16607,19377,16658,25018,4614,12123,11078]"],"out":"376361","g":1},{"in":["[2,2,3,3,1,3,3,1]"],"out":"55","g":1},{"in":["[1,3,3,2,1,2,1,1,1,1]"],"out":"65","g":1},{"in":["[2,3]"],"out":"7","g":1},{"in":["[1,2,2,3,1,3,1,2,2,2,3,1,3,2,3,2,3,1,1,2,2]"],"out":"272","g":1},{"in":["[3,1,3,3,1]"],"out":"23","g":1},{"in":["[3,1,3,3,2]"],"out":"26","g":1},{"in":["[1,3254,4744,8628,8660,9768,13563,22187,22217]"],"out":"300669","g":1},{"in":["[1,3,1,1]"],"out":"12","g":1},{"in":["[10836,4964,30000]"],"out":"60692","g":1},{"in":["[1,1,1,2852,2945,3432,5847,6250,9569,11825,13070,21010,21969,23765,26827,27125,30000,30000,30000]"],"out":"1517147","g":1},{"in":["[2,1,3,2,1,2,1,3,2,1,3,3,1,3,2,1,3,2,3,1,3,2,2,1,3,3,3,3,2,3]"],"out":"532","g":1},{"in":["[12753,2661,20888]"],"out":"44285","g":1},{"in":["[5401,5400,5398,5398,5398,5400]"],"out":"113367","g":1},{"in":["[13827]"],"out":"13827","g":1},{"in":["[3,1,1,3,3,3,2,2,3]"],"out":"75","g":1},{"in":["[21164,24982]"],"out":"67310","g":1},{"in":["[10169,19017,19017,19017,10169,10169,19017,10169]"],"out":"428020","g":1},{"in":["[3,1,1,3,1,3,1,3,3,3,2,3,2,2]"],"out":"146","g":1},{"in":[],"out":"\"#9:6ba1b75b15f0925b\"","perf":{"label":"n = 30,000","gen":"int[] a0 = BCB.ints(30000, 1, 30000);"},"refMs":12}],"lesson":"monotonic-stack","anchor":"sum-of-subarray-minimums--counting-contributions","statement":"For every contiguous subarray of `arr`, take its minimum value. Return the sum of all those minimums, modulo `10^9 + 7`.\n\nEach value is the minimum of every subarray that reaches no further than the nearest smaller value on its left and on its right. Count those subarrays instead of listing them.","constraints":["1 <= arr.length <= 3e4","1 <= arr[i] <= 3e4"],"hints":["Instead of looping over subarrays, ask for each element: in how many subarrays is arr[i] the minimum?","If left[i] elements to the left are strictly greater and right[i] elements to the right are greater or equal, arr[i] is the minimum of left[i] × right[i] subarrays (counting itself on both sides).","Find both counts with monotonic stacks. Use strict < on one side and ≤ on the other so equal values are not counted twice, and add with longs modulo 10⁹ + 7."],"explain":"The 10 subarrays of `[3,1,2,4]` have minimums 3, 1, 2, 4, 1, 1, 2, 1, 1 and 1, which add up to 17."},
